c system imported from USA)\", \"ECMO (Extracorporeal Membrane Oxygenation) critical care programme\", \"ECMO Ambulance Service (mobile life-support transport)\", \"Online Adaptive Radiotherapy on Ethos-Hypersight linear accelerator\", \"Ultrafast 3T MRI imaging including functional/advanced brain imaging\", \"Symbia Pro.specta SPECT CT nuclear medicine imaging\", \"Fully paperless, digitally integrated ICUs with remote monitoring\", \"Free Paediatric Oncology Ward …","promises":[],"promises_total":0,"promoters":[{"name":"Dr. Nalla G Palaniswami","role":"Promoter, Non-Independent & Executive Director; not liable to retire by rotation"},{"name":"Dr. Thavamani Devi Palaniswami","role":"Promoter, Non-Independent & Executive Director; reappointed as Joint Managing Director w.e.f. 29.07.2025 by Special Resolution of shareholders; not liable to retire by rotation"},{"name":"Dr. Arun N Palaniswami","role":"Promoter, Non-Independent & Executive Director"},{"name":"Dr. Mohan S Gounder","role":"Promoter, Non-Independent & Non-Executive Director"},{"name":"Dr. M.C. Thirumoorthi","role":"Promoter, Non-Independent & Non-Executive Director; Paediatric Infectious Diseases specialist on the Board since 16.09.1985, retiring by rotation and seeking re-appointment"},{"name":"Dr. Purani P Palaniswami","role":"Promoter, Non-Independent & Non-Executive Director"}],"related":"[{\"name\": \"Purani Hospital Supplies Private Limited\", \"relation\": \"related party\", \"note\": \"Other related party - entity in which Directors are interested; transactions include purchases\"}, {\"name\": \"Aosta Software Technologies (India) Private Limited\", \"relation\": \"related party\", \"note\": \"Other …","risks":[{"note":"Management states that on account of a multi-fold increase in scale and the expanded area of operations, the Company is exposed to a wide range of internal and external risks and uncertainties that may affect achievement of strategic, operational or financial objectives; its response is a balance of acceptance, avoidance, transfer and mitigation, with greater focus on ring-fencing the organisation from major risks likely to have a lasting impact on profitability and sustainability.","risk":"Scale and expanded operations widen the risk surface"},{"note":"Flagged in the BRSR material-issues table as a risk: non-adherence with standards and guidelines of local and global regulatory agencies, focusing on pharmacovigilance, proprietary, confidentiality and other core governance standards. Mitigation is stated as focusing on stable and larger markets and strengthening regulatory capacity.","risk":"ESG and regulatory compliance"},{"note":"BRSR material issue: a lack of robust controls across the risk management system may lead to adverse impacts across business operations. Mitigation is disaster recovery and business-continuity testing for critical applications and alternative development.","risk":"Weakness in risk-management controls / business continuity"},{"note":"BRSR material issue: inability to meet workforce expectations may impact the Company's retention rate and affect its business. Mitigation is multiple talent-development programmes and a formal succession-planning programme for all leadership positions. Structurally relevant for a hospital where clinical delivery depends on scarce skilled professionals.","risk":"Attracting and retaining talent, and workforce welfare"},{"note":"BRSR material issue: technology risk directly impacts the security and integrity of systems across business operations. Mitigation is strengthened perimeter security and anti-virus/cyber-security measures to reduce risks from cyber attacks and data breaches - material given the Company's move to paperless, digitally integrated ICUs and digital patient records.","risk":"Data integrity, security, technology and digitalisation"},{"note":"Structural concentration disclosed rather than labelled: KMCH's hospitals, peripheral centres (Coimbatore city centre, Sulur, Erode,